  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A square wire loop <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"(w\\times w)\"></span> is moved at a constant velocity <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"v\"></span> (in m s<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"^{-1}\"></span>) through a region of uniform magnetic field <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"B\"></span> (in T). The width of the magnetic field region is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"3w\"></span> (with <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"w\"></span> in m), and the field is perpendicular to the plane of the loop.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p>\n<p>Which graph best represents the variation with time <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"t\"></span> (in s) of the induced electromotive force (emf) <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\varepsilon\"></span> (in V) in the loop as it moves from one side of the magnetic field to the other?</p><ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\">A</li><li data-label=\"B\">B</li><li data-label=\"C\">C</li><li data-label=\"D\">D</li></ol>"
  },
